      "title": "Indemnity dental plans",
      "narration": "An indemnity dental plan lets the patient choose any dentist. A scheduled plan pays a fixed dollar amount per procedure, such as 90 dollars for a filling, and the patient pays the rest; schedules are easy to understand but lag behind rising fees. A nonscheduled plan pays a percentage of usual, customary and reasonable charges by benefit category: typically 100 percent of preventive, 80 percent of basic services such as fillings and extractions, and 50 percent of major services such as crowns and bridges. A combination plan uses a schedule for some services and percentages for others. Dental HMO and PPO networks apply the same categories with network pricing.",
